<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26651" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līmo</span></b> , āre,
			v. a.
		2. limus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bemire, besmirch</i> (in double sense, v. 2.
			limo, I. 2.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 82</span></i>
			.</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> †
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līmo</span></b> ,
				ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λειμών</span>, <i>the Meadow</i>,
			the name of a writing of Cicero, Suet. Vit.
			Ter.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Roman surname</i>: C. Apronius Limo, Ascon. ap.
			Cic. Or. pro Scauro.</div>
